{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst long long MOD = 1000000007LL;\nconst int MAXN = 2000005;\n\nlong long parent[MAXN];\nlong long rankArr[MAXN];\n\nlong long findNode(long long x) {\n    if (parent[x] != x) parent[x] = findNode(parent[x]);\n    return parent[x];\n}\n\nvoid unite(long long a, long long b) {\n    a = findNode(a);\n    b = findNode(b);\n    if (a == b) return;\n    if (rankArr[a] < rankArr[b]) swap(a, b);\n    parent[b] = a;\n    if (rankArr[a] == rankArr[b]) ++rankArr[a];\n}\n\nlong long modPow(long long base, long long exp) {\n    base %= MOD;\n    long long res = 1;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1LL) res = res * base % MOD;\n        base = base * base % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n\n    for (long long i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        parent[i] = i;\n        rankArr[i] = 0;\n    }\n\n    if (m == 0) {\n        cout << modPow(n, n - 1) << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n    if (m == 1) {\n        cout << modPow(n, n) << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    for (long long i = 1; i < n; ++i) {\n        long long bash = (i * m) % n;\n        unite(i, bash);\n    }\n\n    unordered_set<long long> roots;\n    roots.reserve((size_t)n);\n    for (long long i = 1; i < n; ++i) {\n        roots.insert(findNode(i));\n    }\n\n    cout << modPow(n, (long long)roots.size()) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef find(parent, x):\n    # iterative path compression\n    while parent[x] != x:\n        parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]\n        x = parent[x]\n    return x\n\ndef unite(parent, rank, a, b):\n    a = find(parent, a)\n    b = find(parent, b)\n    if a == b:\n        return\n    if rank[a] < rank[b]:\n        a, b = b, a\n    parent[b] = a\n    if rank[a] == rank[b]:\n        rank[a] += 1\n\ndef mod_pow(base, exp):\n    return pow(base, exp, MOD)\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n\n    parent = list(range(n + 1))\n    rank = [0] * (n + 1)\n\n    if m == 0:\n        print(mod_pow(n, n - 1))\n        return\n    if m == 1:\n        print(mod_pow(n, n))\n        return\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        bash = (i * m) % n\n        unite(parent, rank, i, bash)\n\n    roots = set()\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        roots.add(find(parent, i))\n\n    print(mod_pow(n, len(roots)))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00021026308240834624, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0001699779968475923, -5.578839045483619e-05, 0.0, -0.023263266310095787, -0.0034291294869035482, -2.264974000354414e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00014983485743869096, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.029792